# Fork-sync ignore list for PM-Labs/mcp-nanobanana
#
# Format: one upstream commit SHA per line, with a comment on the line above
# explaining why it is permanently rejected. See pmin-mcpinfrastructure
# CLAUDE.md §"Rejecting upstream commits" for the format.
#
# The weekly sync cron (scripts/sync.sh on the droplet) cherry-picks new
# upstream commits; any SHA listed here is skipped permanently.
#
# Additions are welcome — remove entries only when the security concern no
# longer applies. Do NOT remove without re-running the deploy-time review.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Current policy: Pathfinder patches that tighten file-system overreach MUST
# survive fork-sync. The following local changes are NOT commits-to-ignore
# (they are ours, not upstream's), but documenting them here so the next
# operator understands the intent when resolving future cherry-pick conflicts.
#
# Local patches on top of upstream (2026-04-20 deploy-time security review):
#   1. utils/validation_utils.py  — added ensure_inside_image_root() clamp;
#      validate_output_path() now delegates to it.
#   2. tools/generate_image.py    — clamped every input_image_path_* read to
#      IMAGE_OUTPUT_DIR; flipped readOnlyHint False (the tool writes files).
#   3. tests/test_path_security.py — regression test for the clamp.
#
# If an upstream commit touches any of the lines above and conflicts:
#   - Resolve the conflict by KEEPING the clamp behavior (ours), not by
#     reverting to upstream's coarse blocklist or removing readOnlyHint=False.
#   - Do NOT add the upstream commit SHA to this file — just resolve and
#     commit the merge.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

